# PHP conventions

Namespace `CommentEditPro\Includes`. The autoloader maps `Comment_Editing` to `includes/class-comment-editing.php` (lowercase, underscores to hyphens). Admin tabs use `CommentEditPro\Includes\Admin_Tabs`.

Start class files the way existing classes do:

```php
if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
	die( 'No direct access.' );
}
```

New strings use `'comment-edit-pro'`:

```php
__( 'Comment Edit Pro', 'comment-edit-pro' );
```

Settings AJAX checks a feature nonce and a capability together:

```php
if ( ! wp_verify_nonce( $nonce, 'sce-save-advanced-options' ) || ! current_user_can( 'manage_options' ) ) {
	wp_send_json_error(
		array(
			'message' => __( 'Could not verify nonce.', 'comment-edit-pro' ),
		)
	);
}
```

Network screens use `manage_network`. Comment restore, front-end edit, and moderation use `moderate_comments`. Save options through `Options::update_options()` so `sce_options` stays sanitized. Add admin tabs on `comment_edit_pro_admin_tabs`. Extend the free plugin with the `sce_` prefix. Branding filters use `comment_edit_pro_`.

`Init_Tabs::run()` is the list of tabs that load. `Help`, `Appearance`, and `Comment_Actions` sit outside that method.
